  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p25-q25-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Menger sponge",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is constructed by an infinite process starting with a unit cube, and following the instructions below.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p25-q25-step1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Step 1. ",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Divide every face of the cube into nine squares. This sub-divides the cube into 27 smaller cubes.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p25-q25-step2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Step 2. ",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Remove the smaller cube in the middle of each face, and remove the smaller cube in the very centre of the larger cube.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p25-q25-step3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Step 3. ",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Repeat Steps 1 & 2 for each of the remaining smaller cubes, and iterate ad infinitum.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p25-q25-diagram-caption",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The result after four iterations of the above process is shown below.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "image",
        "code": null,
        "src": "/booklet-assets/enrichment-maths-2-part12-20261009/menger-sponge-diagram.png",
        "widthMm": 70,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "retentionReason": "The four-iteration perspective illustration contains thousands of recursively repeated openings and visible tunnel interiors. Retain the original mathematical raster rather than approximate its depth and occlusion.",
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 25,
          "sourceRegion": "Upper right column: Menger sponge illustration only, approximately x=727–1080, y=265–620 in the supplied 1335×1888 image.",
          "description": "Front, top and right faces of the four-iteration Menger sponge, with recursive square openings and central tunnels.",
          "mathematics": "Each retained cube is subdivided into 27 cubes and seven are removed at every iteration.",
          "answerVisibility": "Permanent question illustration; no supplied answers."
        },
        "derived": false
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process there is 1 cube. Find a formula for the number of cubes remaining after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20^n$ cubes.",
          "worked": "Each cube produces $27-7=20$ remaining cubes. Starting with one cube, the number is multiplied by 20 at each iteration:\n$$N_n=20^n.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process there are zero removed cubes. Find a formula for the total number of cubes removed during the first $n$ iterations, counting each removed cube once at the iteration when it is removed.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{7(20^n-1)}{19}$ cubes.\n\nSum the numbers removed at successive iterations.",
          "worked": "At iteration $k$, seven cubes are removed from each of the $20^{k-1}$ remaining cubes. Thus, for $n\\geq1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}R_n&=7(1+20+20^2+\\cdots+20^{n-1})\\\\R_n&=7\\frac{20^n-1}{20-1}\\\\R_n&=\\frac{7(20^n-1)}{19}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe formula also gives $R_0=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process the cube has side length 1. Find a formula for the side length of the smallest cubes in the construction after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac13\\right)^n$.",
          "worked": "Each subdivision divides the side length by 3. Starting with side length 1,\n$$L_n=\\left(\\frac13\\right)^n.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process the total volume that remains is 1. Find a formula for the total volume that remains after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac{20}{27}\\right)^n$.",
          "worked": "There are $20^n$ cubes, each with side length $3^{-n}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}V_n&=20^n\\left(\\frac{1}{3^n}\\right)^3\\\\V_n&=\\left(\\frac{20}{27}\\right)^n.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Let $A_n$ denote the total surface area after $n$ iterations. Explain why this satisfies the recurrence relation\n$$A_{n+1}=\\frac89A_n+24\\times20^n\\times\\left(\\frac19\\right)^{n+1}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac89$ of the existing surface remains. Each of the $20^n$ cubes exposes 24 new faces of area $9^{-(n+1)}$.",
          "worked": "Each existing exposed square face loses its central ninth, leaving $\\frac89A_n$ of the old surface.\n\nInside each retained cube, the removed face-centre cube exposes four side faces. There are six face-centre cubes, giving $6\\times4=24$ new faces. Removing the central cube adds no further exposed faces because its six neighbours are also removed.\n\nThere are $20^n$ retained cubes. Each new face has side length $3^{-(n+1)}$, so its area is $9^{-(n+1)}$. Therefore,\n$$A_{n+1}=\\frac89A_n+24\\times20^n\\times\\left(\\frac19\\right)^{n+1}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q25-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "From this recurrence relation it can be shown that\n$$A_n=4\\left(\\frac89\\right)^n+2\\left(\\frac{20}{9}\\right)^n.$$\nShowing this is beyond the scope of tools we have developed here, however, use this fact to conclude that the total surface area of the Menger sponge is infinite, whilst its volume is finite.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The surface area increases without bound; the volume approaches 0.\n\nUse $\\frac{20}{9}>1$ and $0<\\frac{20}{27}<1$.",
          "worked": "Since $0<\\frac89<1$ and $\\frac{20}{9}>1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}4\\left(\\frac89\\right)^n&\\to0,\\\\2\\left(\\frac{20}{9}\\right)^n&\\to\\infty,\\\\A_n&\\to\\infty.\\end{align*}$$\nFrom part (d),\n$$V_n=\\left(\\frac{20}{27}\\right)^n\\to0$$\nbecause $0<\\frac{20}{27}<1$. Hence the limiting surface area is infinite, while the limiting volume is finite and equals 0.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
